ncealed pung (bad!)\n   - Loses valuable points\n\n**Best Choice:** Play T9 or T8 to eliminate the dead T-suit tiles since T7 has 0 unshown tiles, making T6-T8-T9 combinations impossible. This allows me to focus on the W-suit sequence and the B7 pung.\n\nBetween T9 and T8, playing **T9** is slightly better because it keeps T6-T8 which could theoretically wait for T5 or T7 draws (though T7 is exhausted), while focusing development on W3-W4-W5 sequences.\n\nReason: T7 is completely exhausted (0 unshown), making any T6-T8 or T8-T9 waiting patterns impossible. I should discard T9 to eliminate dead tiles and focus on developing the W3-W4-W5 sequence and maintaining the valuable B7 concealed pung. This maximizes flexibility for forming the remaining melds needed for a winning hand.\n\nAnswer: Play T9"}
